<title>FRANCE: ONIC details EU 96/97 grain intervention stocks.</title>
<headline>ONIC details EU 96/97 grain intervention stocks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union is expected to end the 1996/97 (July/June) season with intervention grain stocks of 2.344 million tonnes against 2.596 million at end-June 1996, figures compiled by France's grain office ONIC show.</p>
<p>The forecast was drawn using data provided by the European Union' agriculture directorate (DG VI) up to June 29.</p>
<p>Provisional situation of European grain intervention stocks on June 29 (in 1,000 tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Soft wheat   Barley  Maize  Rye   Grain total</p>
<p>Opening stock     459	   1,344     0    793     2,596</p>
<p>Vol.offered *     222	     714    13    835     1,783</p>
<p>Vol. sold  **     186	   1,266     0    583     2,035</p>
<p>End stock ***     495	     792    13  1,045     2,344</p>
<p>		 Details by country (in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p>	   Opening stock   Vol.offered*   Vol. sold** End Stock***</p>
<p>Germany     2,432	     1,561	    1,950	2,043</p>
<p>Austria     -			8	     -		  8</p>
<p>Denmark	 68		  48		 64	    53</p>
<p>Spain	    1		   -		  0	     1</p>
<p>Finland	 48		  49		  6	    91</p>
<p>France	  12		  16		 12	    16</p>
<p>Greece	   1		   -		  -	     1</p>
<p>Ireland	  5		  82		  -	    86</p>
<p>Italy	   15		  -		   2	    13</p>
<p>Netherlands   -		   -		   -	     -</p>
<p>Portugal	-		   -		   -	     -</p>
<p>UK		-		   17		  1	    16</p>
<p>Sweden	  14		   3		  -	    17</p>
<p>Benelux	 -		    -		  -	     -</p>
<p>EU-15	2,596		1,783	    2,035	2,344</p>
<p>NOTES: * tonnages offered by farmers for sale to public intervention stores.</p>
<p>** domestic and export sales of intervention grain.</p>
<p>*** after deduction of domestic and export sales.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
